<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.ToolsCard">
  <!-- ══ 常用工具 — a master check box and the list it governs ═══════════════════════════════
       ROUND 8, TASK 6 REPLACED THE ROW GRAMMAR. See AppearanceCard.axaml's header for the argument
       and the published citations for 3 / 7 / 11.

       THIS TAB HAS NO LABEL-AND-CONTROL PAIR AT ALL, so it has no two-column Grid. It has one
       self-labelling check box, one line of instruction, and the list that line points at — which is
       exactly the "all the controls are inside the group" case ctrl-group-boxes says to indicate on
       the larger surface, so there is no group box either and the TabItem carries 常用工具.

       THE MASTER'S LABEL IS ON THE BOX. Round 8, Task 5 made it a CheckBox and took its accessible
       name from ShowToolsTitle through AutomationProperties.LabeledBy, saying its own label would
       move onto it "until Task 6 rewrites the row grammar". This is that move: the title TextBlock
       and the LabeledBy are gone, the Content is the label, and the box names itself.

       THE INSTRUCTION LINE IS NOT A SUBTITLE. It ends in a colon and it introduces the list below it
       ("勾选要在该分类中显示的工具："), which is what keeps it when the four restating subtitles on 外观
       and 行为 were deleted with their AppLanguage keys. It sits 7 below the master (related
       controls) and 3 above the list it labels (the smallest space between a non-interactive control
       and any other control) — both PUBLISHED, vis-layout.

       THE LIST IS DISABLED, NOT HIDDEN, while the master is off — ported verbatim from
       SettingsWindow.BuildToolCheckboxes ("Unchecking only disables the list; the individual states
       stay and are still persisted"): the per-tool Show values keep whatever the user set, so
       re-enabling the category does not silently reset which tools it contains.

       THE LIST BORDER'S OWN 7,5 PADDING AND ITS MaxHeight ARE THE LIST CONTROL'S BUSINESS, not the
       row grammar's, and neither moved in this task. MaxHeight="240" (ported verbatim from
       SettingsWindow's 常用工具 tab) is what keeps a long DefaultTools list — config.json is
       user-editable, see the code-behind — from pushing the tab past the dialog's fixed height.
       Round 7, Task 3's Aero CheckBox template is what gave it room: measured with UI Automation on
       the live surface at 150 %, on the eight tools config.json ships with, on a build with the
       change and a build without —

         each CheckBox   237-339 x 48 physical  ->  1750 x 29   (Auto width -> stretched; 32 -> 19.33 DIP tall)
         row pitch       56 physical            ->  37          (the 3,3 code-set Margin is unchanged)
         list content    8 x 56 = 448 physical  ->  8 x 37 = 296  (299 DIP -> 197 DIP)
         element left    x = 3035 physical      ->  x = 3035    (UNCHANGED)

       — so at 197 DIP the eight fit inside 240 with no scrollbar, and the clamp starts biting at
       roughly twelve tools instead of roughly seven. Those figures were read on the pre-Task-6
       surface and are kept as the LIST's own record; this task did not re-measure them, and the one
       thing it changed around them is what is above the Border, not inside it. -->
  <StackPanel Margin="11">

    <CheckBox x:Name="ShowToolsToggle" IsCheckedChanged="OnShowToolsChanged" />

    <TextBlock x:Name="ToolsListLabel" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,7,0,0" />

    <Border Margin="0,3,0,0" Padding="7,5"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource StrokeControlBrush}" BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="{DynamicResource RadiusControl}">
      <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" MaxHeight="240">
        <StackPanel x:Name="ToolsPanel" />
      </ScrollViewer>
    </Border>
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
